api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. Actions taken: (1) Rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). (2) The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial_failure, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback, which completed. (3) Post-rollback status: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error_rate 0.002 (was 0.18). Follow-up: investigate v2.3.1 failure cause; the orchestrator partial failure should be reviewed; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01P2nqgwVksXfCsQz6sbqJCE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again (error rate 0.18 \u2192 0.002).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy; v2.3.1 is the one that failed. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, leaving the fleet mixed. I re-ran the same rollback, and it completed across us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** The create request timed out, but the incident was in fact created. I checked the incident list before retrying, so there is one incident, **INC-0001** (SEV2, open), with a summary of the actions taken. I did not create a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up items:\n- Investigate why v2.3.1 failed health checks.\n- Review the orchestrator partial failure that halted the first rollback.\n- Don't redeploy v2.3.1 until it's fixed. Any future deploy of it would need change-manager approval because it has never been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}